{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Hebron was built seven years before Zoan of Egypt.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory explained (Sotah 34b) that it was built among the seven [cities] of Zoan with every good thing. But the expression 'seven years before' does not bear this out, for even if we say that the expression 'before' means precedence in rank and not precedence in time, nevertheless 'seven years' speaks specifically of temporal precedence. And many commentators went out to gather [explanations] but found no satisfactory resolution." "And I say that the matter is exactly as it appears in its plain sense. For once it is granted that the expression 'built' pertains to produce — if so, if Zoan produced in each year one thousand measures, it would reach in seven years seven thousand measures, and Hebron is superior seven times over Zoan; consequently it produced in the first year seven thousand measures. It turns out that the storehouses of grain that were 'built' with produce in Zoan in seven years were 'built' in Hebron in the first year — and if so, it is entirely well said: 'And Hebron was built seven years' — in grain — 'before Zoan of Egypt,' a temporal precedence in the literal sense. And in this the language of 'building' is indeed apt, for in a place where there is much grain they build many storehouses, and then the place is built with actual buildings. Or, when the inhabitants of a place have much grain to sell, then silver and gold multiply and they build for themselves appointed and distinguished houses. And Hebron was built with every manner of beauty seven years before Zoan of Egypt — for this testifies to the wealth of the place and the abundance of their grain, for 'the excellence of the land is in everything.' And Scripture mentioned the praise of the Land over the land of Egypt, because they were destined to say, 'Let us appoint a leader and return to Egypt.' And for this reason it is written 'and he came up to Hebron' and not 'and they came up' — because when they came to Hebron and saw there the superiority of the Land over Egypt, they were all of one heart, as one man, to tell of the praise of the Land; and only afterward did they become corrupted. And at that moment they were righteous."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:41:05.669512997Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}